MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1942380753}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: cf5e213db9992e34b9b1eabbd8f92136, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  mainMenuScene: MainMenu
  dialogueText: {fileID: 2053519722}
  endingText: {fileID: 499679035}
  curedPatientsText: {fileID: 1067921893}
  continueButton: {fileID: 452593569}
  dialogueDisplayTime: 3
  letterDelay: 0.05
  goodEndingMusic: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 410870738e2a05a46888ffd099ad07c8, type: 3}
  badEndingMusic: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 839596b02887b6e44a4bc31be9b96c5c, type: 3}
  secretEndingMusic: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 583036dbf04cf424094c991bf1e9a8e3, type: 3}
  overridePatientsCured: 0
  testPatientsCured: 60
  goodDialogue:
  - "The savior stands, silent and still, as the plush-borne gather\u2014threads
    of innocence woven in a solemn unity. Beneath the pale light of the sun, where
    despair and diseased once lingered, a new dawn stirs. In every treatment, a soul
    rekindled. Life, fragile and fleeting, reborn in the quiet seconds betwixt breath
    and mercy. Their hands, vessels of forgotten warmth, reach gently through the
    pale veil. And so the world, once weary and waiting, is wrapped once more in
    a silver light."
  badDialogue:
  - "In a world of dissonance, the doctor stands alone\u2014thy allies, O plush-borne,
    once bright with purpose, now fallen, their threads unspooled by time and consequence.
    Where healing was promised, only ash remains. They do not speak, for what words
    do not remain when all has been undone? The Destructor, born from the lips of
    the broken like a reverent prayer of forgiveness and mercy. Regret clings to
    every breath, a specter of choices made too late. The light has fled, the warmth
    forgotten. Only the cold shallow gasps hope for another destiny."
  secretDialogue:
  - In the climax of miracles achieved beyond measure, a primordial vow hath been
    welcome upon your very existence. Transcension of the ordinary, the tapestry
    of fate woven to the very cusp of the savior, by your hands have intricately 
    sewn life into once broken plush-borne . You, thy chosen, have been worthy of
    such resolution. Savior, thy doctor.
